## 5. chord='None' on a HORIZONTAL-axis card (2 outside Batch 02)

Added 2026-09-07. Scan of all five 03c files for an M3 card holding
`chord = None` while its own `orient = Horizontal`. Four hits corpus-wide;
the two Batch_02 ones (US2009140095A1, US2022266995A1) are being handled in
the current B02 pass, so only these two are left for later.

Two different situations, and the notes already tell them apart:

- **Lateral / anti-torque unit — CORRECT as recorded, do not change.** The
  thrust axis is horizontal but points sideways, so there is no fore/aft
  reading to give. The CHORD `None` description only names the vertical-axis
  case (a lift rotor, a coaxial pair, a hub), which is why this looks wrong
  in the export; the wording, not the record, is what needs widening.

- [x] B03 DE102018116158A1 — boom card, RC, note: "this is a directional
      stabilizer propeller". No action on the data.

- **No note, so it needs the figure.** A horizontal unit on a wing or the
  fuselage with no front/back reading is more likely a genuine "cannot tell"
  (which `None` now legitimately covers since v15.8) — but it could equally be
  a mis-set `orient`. Open it and decide:

- [ ] B05 US2024300644A1 — fuselage card, CVT, no note.

## 6. Vertical rotors mounted BELOW their structure (7) — chord says Front, rule says Back

Added 2026-09-07. Tractor/pusher is about which side of the supporting structure the disc
sits, not about a fore-aft axis: disc ABOVE its structure blows down onto it and the
structure sits in the slipstream (Front / tractor); disc BELOW ingests the structure's wake
(Back / pusher). See CODEBOOK_EDITS.md item 18.

These seven record `orient = Vertical`, `chord = Front`, and a **Ventral** mounting zone —
their own recorded zone contradicts their chord answer. No figure needed to see the
contradiction, but the annotator is checking each one rather than flipping by script.

- [ ] B01 US11072423B1 — hull_array
- [ ] B03 DE202015007089U1 — fuselage
- [ ] B03 DE202016005012U1 — fuselage
- [ ] B04 FR3033363A1 — fuselage
- [ ] B04 IT202300024612A1 — fuselage
- [ ] B04 RU2764311C1 — fuselage
- [ ] B04 US2012056040A1_arch2 — hull_array

> B03 CN109263947A is the eighth ventral card and already reads Back — correct, no action.
> The other ~400 vertical Front/Back cards carry no Dorsal/Ventral zone, so nothing can be
> inferred for them without the figures; they stay as they are under item 18's
> low-confidence note.
